{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793342726,"nonce":"oSREMLYBB+csPiLnuyPwlfjnmJk=","title":"Persist native document IDs and recover closed-draft filesystem moves","message":"Parent: 9d6a14bfc40bc5c2eb5a105609e1c2a1c37f3766d131dae8f4da586edd8b7b3c\nSession epic: ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382\n\nGive native documents persistent opaque identities separate from paths. Bind private recovered graphs to IDs, preserve the saved disk baseline during explicit moves of released unsaved drafts, return path-change receipts, resolve moved IDs and retire IDs on deletion. An old path recreated as another file must not accept its predecessor's recovery or offline vector. Check expected IDs under the same document-open gate as moves.\n\nPersist a bounded checksummed catalog and a filesystem intent before changing entries. Verify filesystem object identities when recovering on either side of interrupted move/remove steps. Exclusive rename must refuse destination collisions. Handle canonical aliases, alias retargeting and case-only moves; refuse a final symlink in draft-preserving moves rather than moving its target. Adopt a single legacy graph without copying its contents; preserve multiple legacy alias graphs for reconciliation.\n\nThis is the native foundation. Active documents still block moves. Browser replica/history identity persistence, hosted recovery-head routing, cross-host identity import, explicit discard/retention, external-writer reconciliation and compute leases remain in the parent. Hosted gateways must advertise this as unavailable and refuse draft-preserving moves until their identity recovery is ready. Do not enable automatic restoration.\n\nValidation includes protocol restart/recreation, dirty saved-baseline preservation, aliases, case changes, symlinks, destination collisions, open-vs-move concurrency, legacy adoption, interrupted filesystem steps, portable core, Windows cross-check and Linux execution on the NUC. Rebuild the browser/session services for local testing after the milestone.","files":null}]}